---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import ImplDrills from '../components/ImplDrills.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Implementation drills', description: 'Short coding exercises for the bugs that cost contest time without being hard.' }}>
  <p>
    Most lost minutes in a contest come from small implementation bugs, not from missing ideas: a loop that reads one value too many,
    an array that is not reset between test cases, a division that rounds the wrong way, a midpoint that overflows. Each drill below
    takes 3 to 5 minutes. Set a timer, write the solution yourself without looking, then open the reference and compare.
  </p>
  <p>
    A drill appears here and at the end of the first lesson that has everything it needs, under "Check yourself". This is the
    <strong>Implementation bug</strong> category of the <a href={url('/method/')}>Method</a> page: when you log that mistake, come back
    and redo the matching drill. The reference solutions are tested against a brute force; the drills are not topics and are not part of any checkpoint.
  </p>
  <p>
    More practice of the same kind lives on two other pages: the <a href={url('/volume/')}>Volume set</a> (easy problems for speed and clean code) and the <a href={url('/bridge/')}>Bridge set</a> (rating 1900 to 2100, from Phase 4 towards Phase 5).
  </p>
  <ImplDrills />
</StarlightPage>
